From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xe Chromium Patches <noreply@xe.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:57:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/50] direct route: maxFrameRate caps the guest's own frame rate

- content::SetFrameSinkIntervalForRequester: per frame sink, every
  requester (the embedder's setFrameRate(), each GuestFrameTextureSource)
  keeps its own requested BeginFrame interval; the longest (lowest rate)
  is applied; clearing one restores the others.
- CreateSource(max_frame_rate): a source with a maxFrameRate requests
  that interval for its guest while alive (combined with back-pressure:
  the lower rate wins), so a cap means fewer guest frames and one copy per
  guest frame. Blink no longer gates requests by time (that under-delivered
  under load: 30 -> 19.9 at N = 32).
---
